+  // The reported bug (stoplightio/spectral#2638) is that the `array-items` rule
+  // threw `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'type')` while
+  // traversing documents that contain `null` values. The contract only requires
+  // that validation completes without that crash; it does not require the rule
+  // to be extended to additional document formats. These cases therefore assert
+  // the rule's normal diagnostics on a document that also contains `null`
+  // values, which is enough to reject the crashing implementation while
+  // accepting any null-safe implementation.
+  {
+    name: 'array items sibling is missing in a oas2 document',
+    document: {
+      openapi: '3.0.0',
+      paths: {
+        '/path': {
+          get: {
+            responses: {
+              '200': {
+                description: null,
+                content: {
+                  'application/json': {
+                    schema: {
+                      type: 'array',
+                    },
+                  },
+                },
+              },
+            },
+          },
+        },
+      },
+    },
+    errors: [
